 "review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "round": 1,
  "problems": [
   "The rainbow fan is the main story beat, but it barely shows. It's a narrow wedge, about 15\u00b0 wide, coming off the right side of the prism. In the 'in a place' and 'wide' shots it shrinks to a thin striped sliver beside the plinth. It does not read as a fan of colour spread across the ground.",
   "The fan rises steeply through the air from y=-176 and only touches the floor at its far tip (x\u2248116\u2013150). The brief says the rainbow fans across the ground and light pulses visibly travel along the floor. Right now the 'flow' lines run down the steep fan edge, not along the floor, and the floor pool (ellipse at 132,4, a 0.18) can hardly be seen.",
   "Stray shape: the 'pale' line from (20,-250) to (30,-110) at a 0.4 reads as a thin brown stick or wire floating beside the prism in the close-up. It is not attached to any facet.",
   "The pulsing white ellipse in the middle of the prism (4,-182, rx10, ry34) reads as a floating blob or slot, not as an inner glow where the beam refracts.",
   "For a hero landmark the prism is only about as tall as the person (\u2248340 vs a person of \u2248200\u2013220, which is acceptable). The plinth is low and thin: 56 tall plus a 16 cap. Next to the figure it reads like a small pedestal, not a monument base."
  ]
 },
 "for": "Tall faceted glass prism on a stone plinth that splits a beam into a rainbow fan across the ground. It is the hero landmark, and its light pulses travel visibly",
